  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to my estate after a "merger" meeting.
    - Resident returning to the high-security district.
    - Collecting a private shipment of "medical supplies".
    midDaysReasons:
    - Relocating assets to a more secure underground vault.
    - Checking on the loyalty of my remaining "employees".
    - Seeking shelter in my private reinforced bunker.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to assigned bunk for the final lockdown.
    - Seeking refuge from the falling black ash.
    - Fulfilling mandatory residency check-in for executives.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Going to the park to feed the pigeons for six hours.
    - Buying a bus ticket to a city that was nuked yesterday.
    - Applying for a job as a low-level janitor at the mall.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning to a warehouse that was seized by the military.
    - Buying a wedding ring for a woman I never met.
    - Going to the tax office to report my illegal earnings.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to prepare for my 100th birthday party.
    - I need to find the man who sold me a broken sun.
    - To see if the police still remember how to bleed.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "You look nervous, officer. Relax. I\u2019m just a businessman coming home."
    - "Here are the papers. Make sure you don't smudge the ink; I\u2019m a man who
      likes things clean."
    - You have a difficult job. It would be a shame if something made it even harder
      for you.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - The world is changing, but men like me? We always find a way to stay on top.
    - "Don't look at the sky, look at me. I\u2019m the one who decides if you have
      a good night."
    - "Is there a problem with the date? I\u2019m sure we can reach an... understanding."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Even when this city is ash, I will still be the one holding the shovel.
    - "Stamping that paper is the smartest thing you\u2019ll do all day. Don't disappoint
      me."
    - "I\u2019m going home to count what\u2019s left. Get out of my way."
