  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2bd959cca4ad2c849aa7515fa6f29923, type: 3}
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2b0d28dc1905fe4478aee2c13c77d063, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The docks. Import work. Standard.
    midDaysAnswer: The docks are restricted. I've been working on getting clearance.
    finalDaysAnswer: Around. I don't say more than I need to.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The office. Clean work. No docks, no shipments. Just
      paperwork. Everything above board.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The office. I've always run a legitimate operation. The
      docks are not relevant to my work.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The docks. Full access. No restrictions. Everything
      is proceeding as normal. Nothing to report.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. I'm healthy.
    midDaysAnswer: I've been coughing. The air near the docks is bad.
    finalDaysAnswer: I don't answer questions like that.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: A cough, yes. Came on recently. I'm looking into the
      cause. Could be environmental.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No cough. My lungs are fine. I stay away from the docks
      precisely because of the air.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. Perfectly healthy. I take care of myself. No
      issues of any kind.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Colleagues. We rotate.
    midDaysAnswer: Two men. We watch each other's backs.
    finalDaysAnswer: That's not your business.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My wife and our two boys. North hill. Private residence.
      That's all you need to know.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Alone. I don't trust colleagues enough to share a roof.
      Never have.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My wife and my sons. At home. Safe. That is not your
      concern.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Smart uniform. I hope there is a smart man wearing it.
    - Take your time, officer. I am a patient man. Ask anyone who works for me.
    - You have a family, I assume. Hold onto that.
    midDays:
    - The city is reorganizing. Smart people are already choosing sides.
    - I own three blocks that used to belong to the state. Funny how that works out.
    - You are still at your post. Good. That means you are useful.
    finalDays:
    - When the dust settles, I will still be here. Will you?
    - Stamp the paper, officer. We both know who actually runs this gate.
    - I control what is left. That is not a threat. It is simply a fact.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
